WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
On framed cotton, draw a leaf about 4 cm long.
Mark the centre vein and three guides on each side.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.300
Stitch the centre vein with the Aari hook.
Catch the thread from below and link each new loop.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.700
Stitch the guides closest to the vein first.
Work outward, one row at a time.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.800
Use shorter loops where the leaf narrows.
Keep neighbouring rows beside each other.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.000
Remove the swatch from the frame.
Check that the cloth lies flat and the rows stay even.
